{
  "UniqueID": "act_tool_belt",
  "CardName": {
    "ParentObjectID": "act_tool_belt",
    "LocalizationKey": "Advanced_Copper_Tools_ToolBelt_CardName",
    "DefaultText": "Copper-Buckled Tool Belt"
  },
  "CardDescription": {
    "ParentObjectID": "act_tool_belt",
    "LocalizationKey": "Advanced_Copper_Tools_ToolBelt_CardDescription",
    "DefaultText": "A broad leather belt closed with a copper buckle, with six tool slots: loops for hammers, knives, chisels, sickles and spoon augers, a pouch for a whetstone or a fire striker, and a needle case. It has a Tool Belt slot of its own, so it never takes the place of a knife sheath, a spear sheath or any other gear. Tools carried in it weigh less and still count as on you. MUST BE EQUIPPED ON EQUIPMENT SLOT TO WORK."
  },
  "CardHelpSection": {
    "ParentObjectID": "act_tool_belt",
    "LocalizationKey": "Advanced_Copper_Tools_ToolBelt_CardHelpSection",
    "DefaultText": "<b>Crafted:</b> From 1 copper sheet, 1 medium leather and 4 copper nails using a hammer.\n\n<b>Uses:</b> Equip it on the Tool Belt slot, one belt at a time. It does not use the slot of a knife sheath or a spear sheath, so you can wear all three. It holds hammers, knives, chisels, sickles and spoon augers, a whetstone or a fire striker, and needles, and takes 200 off their combined weight. A tool in it still counts as on you for an action that looks for one.\n\n<b>Blueprints:</b> a blueprint's ingredient slot does not take tools from your belt. Drag the hammer out of it onto the blueprint, as you always have."
  },
